  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Triptolidenol and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of target interactions involving Dynamin-1. Triptolidenol is identified as a target of Dynamin-1, which in turn is a target of two different compounds: Olean-13(18)-ene-3beta,11alpha-diol and Dihydroepoxyalantolactone. Both of these compounds are linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, indicating a possible pathway through which Triptolidenol may influence the enzyme. The scores from the three paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological connection, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential regulatory role of Triptolidenol in modulating UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
